# An allowlist, not a denylist. The image is built from exactly four paths
# (Dockerfile: the two COPY lines for graphite-core/Cargo.{toml,lock}, then
# graphite-core/src and graphite-core/protocols), so the build context is
# exactly those four paths and nothing else. A denylist has to anticipate every
# local directory that could appear — nested target/ and node_modules/, local
# graphite-data/ audit trails, agent session directories, scratch output — and
# Docker's matcher anchors `target/` at the root, so the old list missed the
# nested ones (A6-12). Anything not re-included below never reaches the
# builder. A new COPY in the Dockerfile needs a matching `!` line here, and
# the CI container job fails loudly if one is missing.
*
!graphite-core/Cargo.toml
!graphite-core/Cargo.lock
!graphite-core/src
!graphite-core/protocols
